  "details": "The new HUD has been e̶n̶o̶r̶m̶o̶u̶s great so far, and I think it's great that we can toggle it so easily. However, the only issue I've noticed is that hiding the new HUD doesn't hide the new [massive] interactive object/pickup tooltips [that now cover the right side of the screen despite already also appearing on the highlighted object].\n\nI'm aware that a new setting has been added to toggle these, and that the entire client crashes every time I search for \"contextual\" or \"con\" in settings (until I swap to a non-zero tab like User Interface, then search something else like \"mirror\", THEN search for \"contextual\"), so that's a good start, but I feel like this solution alone is a bit counter-intuitive; I feel like hiding the HUD should also hide the interactive object/pickup tooltips that were implemented along with that HUD, that also share the same style and scaling as that HUD, and whose toggle setting is categorized under \"Desktop HUD\" in settings.\n\nThe granular toggles are good, I like that I can toggle each HUD aspect individually, but I just think hiding the entire HUD should hide the entire HUD.",
